# DaVinci Resolve Scripting Docs

Whenever a task touches DaVinci Resolve, Resolve scripting, `/color`, Resolve export, DRX/DRT,
LUT automation, Resolve render jobs, Resolve groups, color node graphs, or the vendored Resolve
host, first read:

- `.ai/knowledge/davinci-resolve-scripting.md`

Then verify any version-sensitive method against the installed official Resolve scripting docs:

- macOS: `/Library/Application Support/Blackmagic Design/DaVinci Resolve/Developer/Scripting/README.txt`
- Windows: `%PROGRAMDATA%\Blackmagic Design\DaVinci Resolve\Support\Developer\Scripting\README.txt`
- Linux: `/opt/resolve/Developer/Scripting/README.txt`

The user-requested online mirror is:

- `https://gist.github.com/X-Raym/2f2bf453fc481b9cca624d7ca0e19de8`

## Hard Rules

- Do not implement Resolve scripting behavior from memory when a local/API doc check is possible.
- Do not treat the Gist as merely a link index; Kairos' local doc is the working document.
- Do not claim unsupported API behavior exists unless it is present in the installed docs or proven by live Resolve introspection.
- Do not claim color node enabled/readback state from `SetNodeEnabled()` alone; official docs expose `SetNodeEnabled()` but not `GetNodeEnabled()`.
- Do not claim an OFX such as Gyroflow has loaded source-specific data merely because `GetToolsInNode()` shows the OFX shell.
- Prefer live-verified clean DRT donor paths over DRX-only assumptions for Gyroflow source loading; a DRX repair template is layout evidence, not load evidence, unless a live probe proves otherwise.
- If live Resolve verification is required, report the exact project/timeline/clips used.
